+## 2026-10-24 biaxial teaching repair
+
+Version 2.2.0 could assemble three default demonstrations that were all
+symmetric about one input axis while the query was not. Two wrong rules then fit
+every demonstration and failed the query:
+
+- mirror vertically, but repeat each row instead of left/right mirroring it;
+- mirror horizontally, but repeat the top half instead of up/down mirroring it.
+
+The retained v2.2 counterexamples use seeds 578 and 742. Version 2.3.0 keeps the
+canonical output rule unchanged and adds a default-only curriculum witness on
+every even sample index. Three sampled cells make one horizontal mirror pair and
+one vertical mirror pair unequal while preserving dimensions and the palette
+envelope. Every three consecutive default samples therefore contains a draw
+that refutes both single-axis shortcuts. Explicit overrides, including the
+intentional degenerate texture controls, keep their prior behavior.
+
+Verification: 12 focused/task tests passed. The reusable bounded probe checked
+10,240 consecutive three-demonstration lessons across default/easy/medium/hard,
+20,480 competitor fits, and found zero demonstration survivors. This finite
+two-rival audit is not a uniqueness proof.
